UNIT nintendo_password_hash
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
FIDELITY spec
ANCHOR the password hash a Wii U sends to the account server instead of the password (Pretendo account server, and the values Python's hashlib gives for the same bytes)
SIG nintendo_password_hash(pid: u64, password: text) -> text
ENVELOPE pid is 0 to 4294967295; password is any well-formed text.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION The hash a console sends for an account's password: the server checks it without ever seeing the password.
BEHAVIOR
R1 The bytes hashed are: pid as four bytes, least significant first; then the four bytes 02 65 43 46; then password as UTF-8. CITED
R2 The answer is the SHA-256 of those bytes, written as 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits. CITED
PROVENANCE recorded by rdv from accounts/accounts.go
ORACLE value -> oracles/nintendo_password_hash.json CANONICAL-SHA256 cb1c151998b8e2e5bc3761cc7c1a8d977bb6cc4460d64a3da3b490aba84d0d76
NOTE rules written; no independent rebuild has been graded yet.
